{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:870a8ca1767fb91c","name":"Intercept Communications","source":{"id":"source:reference-870a8ca1767fb91c","title":"Intercept Communications","revision":18724,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:37:42Z","sha256":"2d0e814504e540d03c825553fc4d0444fd62c7a1c11d1fa3fc8621757618a64f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18724","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Intercept%20Communications&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-870a8ca1767fb91c","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", you can attempt to Intercept Communications between two other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},". If the other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," take no special precautions, this is a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check; otherwise, the DC is set by the higher of their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check results for securing communications (see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Communications"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Communications","referenceId":"reference:fa12b21dc3aa7266"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Furthermore, if the other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," are using encrypted communications systems (such as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Comlink","referenceId":"reference:609e72c37493843f"}," (Encrypted) or ",{"tag":"a","children":["IFF Transponders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/IFF_Transponders"}," with matching encryption codes), add 10 to the DC. If your check result fails by 10 or less when attempting to intercept encrypted communications, you can identify what encryption protocols they are using. (\"It might be an Imperial Code.\")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
